      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has limited room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing part of the Mo with Nb will enhance room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::012::3_results"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing part of the Mo with Nb will cause only a slight reduction in strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::012::3_results"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is to replace 10–20 atomic percentage points of Mo with additional Nb.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloys will retain a single-phase BCC matrix with minimal change in phase constitution.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo increases lattice friction and barriers to dislocation slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo increases strength and decreases toughness or fracture strain in related refractory high-entropy alloys.",
